🚀 **Laravel Project Deployed on AWS EC2 | Terraform + GitHub Actions CI/CD**

I’m excited to share one of my recent DevOps projects — a **Laravel application deployed on an AWS EC2 server** with Infrastructure as Code and a CI/CD pipeline. ☁️

🔹 **Infrastructure as Code — Terraform**
First, I provisioned the complete AWS infrastructure using **Terraform** instead of creating resources manually.

This makes the infrastructure **reproducible and scalable** — whenever required, a DevOps engineer can recreate the same infrastructure by running the Terraform configuration again.

🔹 **CI/CD Pipeline — GitHub Actions**
I also implemented a **CI/CD pipeline using GitHub Actions** to automate the application deployment process.

The workflow helps automate the process from code changes to deployment on the EC2 server, reducing manual work and making deployments more consistent.

🔹 **Technologies Used**
• Laravel / PHP
• AWS EC2
• Terraform
• GitHub Actions
• Git & GitHub
• Linux / Ubuntu
• CI/CD
• Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

💡 **Key DevOps Concept:**
Instead of manually setting up the server and infrastructure every time, the infrastructure is defined as code. This means it can be **created, destroyed, and recreated whenever needed** using Terraform.

